    "review_notes": [
      "Kernel32 additions are legacy Win32 loading, formatting, process and x64 SEH APIs available before the Vista target; GetProcAddress and GetModuleHandleW support the libc++ time fallback.",
      "CRT additions are exports of the existing UCRT API-set l1-1-0 contracts (heap/runtime/stdio/string/filesystem/math/convert), not additional runtime DLLs.",
      "The precise-time API is deliberately absent from both lists; a mandatory import must fail the gate. Native runtime smoke remains required evidence separate from this allowlist."
    ]
